## 7. Key Implementation Details

### 7.1 Location Grid Component
- 10 number inputs per row, all default to 0
- Real-time auto-sum into TOTAL column
- Real-time LINE TOTAL = TOTAL × QAR price
- Section subtotal updates on every input change
- Tab key should flow left-to-right across locations, then down to next item
- Green background `#C6EFCE` on all input cells
- Items with no qty ordered can be visually dimmed

### 7.2 Heavy Machinery Component
- Group forklifts by tonnage (3T, 5T, 7T, 10T) with visual separators
- Each rental row: QTY input + MAST dropdown + START date + END date
- Auto-compute DAYS and LINE TOTAL
- Fork extension rows appear below their parent forklift group
- Golf buggies at the bottom (no mast dropdown)
- Validate: if QTY > 0, dates must be filled

### 7.3 Surcharge Logic
```javascript
const isPastCutoff = new Date() > new Date(cutoffDate);
const surchargeRate = isPastCutoff ? 0.10 : 0;
const adjustedTotal = grandTotal * (1 + surchargeRate);
```
Show warning banner if past cut-off. The at-venue 20% surcharge is informational only (applied manually at the venue).

### 7.4 Form State Management
Use React `useReducer` or a form library (React Hook Form) to manage:
- All 90+ catalog items × 10 locations = ~900 quantity fields
- 31 heavy machinery items with mixed field types
- Contact details
- Performance matters — debounce recalculations or use `useMemo`

### 7.5 Export to Matrix (Import Bridge)
The admin side needs an "Import to Matrix" button per submission that:
1. Reads the submission JSON
2. Opens the corresponding matrix `.xlsx` (from the LIC-FFE project's data folder)
3. Finds or creates the team's column
4. Writes each item's totalQty to the matching row
5. For heavy machinery, writes qty (and optionally dates/mast as a note)
6. Saves the matrix
7. Marks the submission as "imported"

